BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:white-rabbit-gallery-wrg-digital-generation-xi-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T152857Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: WRG Digital Call-Out: Generation Xi (White Rabbit Gallery
 )
DESCRIPTION:White Rabbit Gallery in Sydney commissions an emerging artist o
 r designer to create a short digital animation responding to its Generatio
 n Xi exhibition\, which looks at China's youth amid the AI\, robotics and 
 EV revolution\, and to the New Ugly digital design aesthetic. The commissi
 oned work (up to 20 seconds\, minimum 1280x720 at 16:9\, max 150MB\, inclu
 ding the exhibition title in English and Mandarin) is displayed for five m
 onths on the gallery's website landing page and enters the permanent WRG D
 igital Archive. SUPPORT: AUD 2\,000 artist fee (split equally if a collabo
 rative group) plus mentorship from creative agency Spring in Alaska during
  the development period (28 September - 2 November 2026). ELIGIBILITY: ope
 n internationally to applicants 18+ within the first 10 years of their art
 istic or design practice who are not represented by a commercial gallery o
 r design agency and not employed by a design company\; students and collec
 tives welcome. Free to enter. Deadline: 14 September 2026\, 5pm AEST.\n\nO
 rganisation: White Rabbit Gallery\nLocation: Online (gallery in Sydney\, A
 ustralia)\; no travel required\nAward: AUD 2\,000 artist fee (split equall
 y if a collaborative group)\; free to enter\nDuration: Development period 
 28 September - 2 November 2026 with mentorship\; commissioned work display
 ed 5 months on the gallery website plus permanent WRG Digital Archive incl
 usion\n\nMore: https://whiterabbitcollection.org/wrg-digital-call-out/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://whiterabbitcollection.org/wrg-digital-call-out/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (gallery in Sydney\, Australia)\; no travel required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:making-space-guangzhou-nl-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T152857Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Deadline: Making Space Residency 2027 for Netherlands-Based Practit
 ioners (Guangzhou)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in China\, in par
 tnership with artist-run space Making Space in Guangzhou\, invites Netherl
 ands-based artists\, makers\, curators\, writers\, researchers and other c
 ultural practitioners to a six-week residency in spring 2027. Making Space
  (est. 2017) focuses on art and social practice with an emphasis on long-t
 erm research\, local knowledge and care-driven collaboration. The residenc
 y is process-oriented with no obligation to produce finished work\; the re
 sident takes part in at least one public exchange (talk\, workshop\, readi
 ng group\, screening\, performance or open studio). SUPPORT: EUR 2\,700 tr
 avel and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives s
 hare the amount)\, accommodation in Guangzhou\, shared studio space\, cura
 torial and research support with access to local networks\, and logistical
  support for public programming (extra funding may be considered for publi
 c programmes). The resident arranges their own China visa\; Making Space p
 rovides an invitation letter. LOOKING FOR: practitioners engaging with alt
 ernative education\, ecological justice\, migration and labour\, social pr
 actice\, intergenerational narratives\, diaspora and transdisciplinary col
 laboration\; English communication required. APPLY by email (makingspace20
 17@gmail.com) with a 200-word bio\, CV\, 2-page project proposal and portf
 olio (max 20 pages) in a single PDF\, in English. Result expected late Nov
 ember 2026. Deadline: 3 October 2026\, 23:59 CST / 17:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Making Space\, in partnership with the Embassy of the Kingdom of the
  Netherlands in China\nLocation: Guangzhou\, China\nAward: EUR 2\,700 trav
 el and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives sha
 re it)\, plus accommodation in Guangzhou and shared studio space\nDuration
 : Six continuous weeks between 15 March and 15 June 2027\, dates agreed wi
 th the selected resident\n\nMore: https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Guangzhou\, China
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T152857Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi Museum: SIXI AiR Open Call 2027 Spring & Autumn (Nan
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:The Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project\, run by Six
 i Museum in Nanjing since 2024\, selects 4 artists across two three-month 
 sessions in 2027 (Spring\, March to May\, and Autumn\, September to Novemb
 er). The program is built as an open network across the city\, connecting 
 residents with local scholars\, artists\, historic neighborhoods and natur
 al landscapes\, with Open Studios and workshops along the way. Proposals m
 ust respond to one of two themes: Flux and Imprints\, Contemporary Echoes 
 of Migration History (cross-regional mobility\, cultural reconstruction an
 d memory\, including family histories of overseas Chinese\, the legacy of 
 colonialism in Asia\, and identity within global geopolitics)\, or Folds o
 f Text\, Cross-Media Intertextuality and Intervention (text as a fluid med
 ium\, with interdisciplinary work across literature\, linguistics\, music 
 and sound\, and visual arts). SUPPORT: round-trip flights\, visa fees\, in
 surance\, private apartment or loft studio\, material allowance\, technica
 l assistance\, airport pickup and translation\; no separate artist fee or 
 stipend is mentioned. ELIGIBILITY: artists of all disciplines\, aged 18 or
  older\, proficient in spoken and written Mandarin or English. HOW TO APPL
 Y: email a CV with profile photo\, portfolio and residency proposal as a s
 ingle PDF or ZIP with the subject line Residency Application. Final respon
 ses by mid-February 2027\; allow 2 to 3 months for visa processing. DEADLI
 NE: 15 November 2026 (GMT+8).\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: Nanj
 ing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural backgrounds\,
  aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.\nAward: Round-trip 
 flights\, visa application fees\, insurance\, and a private city-center ap
 artment or loft studio on the outskirts\, plus a material allowance (amoun
 t not published)\, technical assistance\, airport pickup and translation s
 upport. NO artist fee or stipend mentioned. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Three months: Spring 2027 (March to May) or Autumn 2027 (September to Nov
 ember).\n\nMore: https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural b
 ackgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:matsu-biennial-4-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T152857Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: 4th Matsu Biennial International Open Call (Matsu Islands
 \, Taiwan)
DESCRIPTION:The 4th Matsu Biennial invites artists and creative teams world
 wide to develop new work for the Matsu Islands\, Taiwan\, taking the archi
 pelago itself as its site: its geography\, Cold War history\, marine ecolo
 gy and everyday life. No single theme is set\; proposals can explore three
  axes: The Island (Eastern Min culture\, religious practices\, traditional
  stone houses\, the returning generation)\, The Outpost (site translation\
 , geopolitics\, blackout regulations\, collective memory) and The Ocean (e
 nvironmental care\, sustainable ecology\, blue tears sea sparkles\, marine
  debris). PROJECT TYPES: site-specific installations\, indoor or outdoor\,
  produced on site\; and participatory creative projects such as interdisci
 plinary actions\, immersive experiences or community interactions. SUPPORT
 : 4 to 5 proposals are selected\, each in principle receiving NTD 800\,000
  (approx. USD 25\,000\, tax included). Works must be completed by 10 Augus
 t 2027\; the exhibition runs 20 August to 7 November 2027. ELIGIBILITY: in
 dividuals and teams of any nationality\, aged 18 and over\; up to two prop
 osals per applicant\; existing works may be reworked if they respond to Ma
 tsu's site conditions and cultural context\; artists may choose from sugge
 sted sites across Nangan\, Beigan\, Dongju and Xiju or propose their own. 
 HOW TO APPLY: online via Google Form with a project proposal in Chinese or
  English (PDF\, max 8 pages\, 10 MB)\, an artist CV/portfolio (PDF\, max 5
  pages\, 10 MB\, at least 3 previous works)\, and a signed copyright licen
 se agreement. Results announced by the end of November 2026. DEADLINE: 30 
 October 2026 at 17:00 (GMT+8).\n\nOrganisation: Matsu Biennial Promotion C
 ommittee (Lienchiang County Government and General Association of Chinese 
 Culture)\nLocation: Matsu Islands (Nangan\, Beigan\, Dongju\, Xiju)\, Taiw
 an. Open to individual artists\, creative practitioners and artist teams o
 f any nationality\, aged 18 and over.\nAward: 4 to 5 proposals are selecte
 d\; each in principle receives NTD 800\,000 (approximately USD 25\,000\, t
 ax included) in financial support.\nDuration: Selected works must be compl
 eted by 10 August 2027\; exhibition planned 20 August to 7 November 2027\n
 \nMore: https://matsubiennial.tw/en/news/details/88?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://matsubiennial.tw/en/news/details/88?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Matsu Islands (Nangan\, Beigan\, Dongju\, Xiju)\, Taiwan. Open to 
 individual artists\, creative practitioners and artist teams of any nation
 ality\, aged 18 and over.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mplus-sigg-fellowship-chinese-art-research-2026-27@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T152857Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: M+ Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research 2026/27 (HKD 
 200\,000\, Hong Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research supports new resea
 rch on Chinese art in dialogue with the M+ Collections\; the 2026/27 editi
 on focuses on tradition and contemporary Chinese art. WHO: individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality and any age\, with a postgraduate degre
 e in a relevant discipline\, or an undergraduate degree plus at least thre
 e years of relevant professional or academic research experience\; profici
 ency in spoken and written Chinese or English is required\, and the fellow
 ship is subject to obtaining a Hong Kong visa. WHAT YOU GET: HKD 200\,000 
 to cover all expenses\, including travel\, living\, insurance and research
  costs\, for a three-to-six-month attachment to M+. Fellows give a public 
 lecture in Hong Kong and write an essay of at least 5\,000 English words o
 r 7\,500 Chinese characters for M+ Magazine. APPLICATION: submit a researc
 h proposal (max 1\,000 words) and full CV via the Google form on the call 
 page\, in English or Chinese\, and have two academic or professional refer
 ees email recommendation letters directly. Results are announced in early 
 2027. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026\, 23:59 (UTC+8).\n\nOrganisation: M+\, We
 st Kowloon Cultural District\nLocation: Hong Kong. Open to individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a
  Hong Kong visa.\nAward: HKD 200\,000 covering all expenses (travel\, livi
 ng\, insurance and research costs). No application fee mentioned.\nDuratio
 n: 3 to 6 months attached to M+ in Hong Kong.\n\nMore: https://www.mplus.o
 rg.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-chinese-art-research/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-
 chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
LOCATION:Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationali
 ty\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
